WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.470 --> 00:00:02.139
Speaker 1: . Now, many of you have been asking.

00:00:02.139 --> 00:00:05.669
It's covid going to become a Republican virus.

00:00:05.669 --> 00:00:08.810
Is this going to become a Republican pandemic
in the United States?

00:00:08.810 --> 00:00:14.410
Because when you look at the numbers, if Democrats
are getting vaccinated at way higher rates

00:00:14.410 --> 00:00:20.390
than Republicans and if blue states have much
more cautious rules about large indoor gatherings,

00:00:20.390 --> 00:00:25.150
et cetera, then red states, won't it eventually
become a Republican pandemic?

00:00:25.150 --> 00:00:28.710
And the answer is that it overwhelmingly already
is.

00:00:28.710 --> 00:00:34.610
We have new numbers that Philip Bump wrote
about in The Washington Post, which showed

00:00:34.610 --> 00:00:42.350
that the new infection rate in the last couple
of weeks is twice as high per capita in red

00:00:42.350 --> 00:00:46.220
counties than it is in blue counties in the
United States.

00:00:46.220 --> 00:00:51.400
So important, this is at the county level,
way more precise than the state level.

00:00:51.400 --> 00:00:56.350
You know, the thing about looking at the state
level is you can have a blue state that's

00:00:56.350 --> 00:01:01.240
53 to 46, a state that Joe Biden won.

00:01:01.240 --> 00:01:06.860
But you might really have a much more precise
division if you look at red and blue counties

00:01:06.860 --> 00:01:08.210
within that state.

00:01:08.210 --> 00:01:12.820
Now, some of the counties might only be slightly
blue or slightly red, but it's a much more

00:01:12.820 --> 00:01:15.740
accurate and precise way of slicing and dicing
this.

00:01:15.740 --> 00:01:17.400
And the numbers are shocking.

00:01:17.400 --> 00:01:24.760
In the last two weeks, on average, blue counties
are seeing 10 new cases per 100000 residents,

00:01:24.760 --> 00:01:30.570
whereas red counties are seeing 20 new cases
per 100000 residents.

00:01:30.570 --> 00:01:36.620
The new case rate in red counties counties
that voted Trump rather than Biden is twice

00:01:36.620 --> 00:01:40.680
that of the new case rate in Biden counties.

00:01:40.680 --> 00:01:43.100
That is a stunning gap.

00:01:43.100 --> 00:01:47.770
And it's actually you can make the case that
the numbers don't even tell you how bad it

00:01:47.770 --> 00:01:53.150
is, because when you consider that blue counties
tend to be more densely populated than red

00:01:53.150 --> 00:01:54.610
counties.

00:01:54.610 --> 00:02:00.490
This reflects very poorly on red counties,
like the default position for positivity rates

00:02:00.490 --> 00:02:04.950
is that red counties should be doing better
than blue counties, all else being equal because

00:02:04.950 --> 00:02:06.290
you have a lower population density.

00:02:06.290 --> 00:02:10.920
It should be a little more difficult for it
to spread when the population density is lower.

00:02:10.920 --> 00:02:17.420
The fact that the new case rate is twice as
high in red counties, even despite having

00:02:17.420 --> 00:02:19.760
lower population density, is incredible.

00:02:19.760 --> 00:02:25.980
Now, the other important thing is the Delta
variant, which is significantly more contagious.

00:02:25.980 --> 00:02:30.900
The Delta variant is affecting the whole country,
red and blue states, red and blue counties,

00:02:30.900 --> 00:02:31.900
everybody.

00:02:31.900 --> 00:02:33.630
Everybody's affected by the delta variant.

00:02:33.630 --> 00:02:39.910
But if you consider and compare counties today
versus where they were a year ago, meaning

00:02:39.910 --> 00:02:45.739
not only pre Delta but pre vaccine, we are
basically seeing the same partizan split on

00:02:45.739 --> 00:02:46.739
average.

00:02:46.739 --> 00:02:52.209
You see even even consider it comparing to
a year ago, you are seeing dramatically worse

00:02:52.209 --> 00:02:54.800
numbers in the red counties than in the blue
counties.

00:02:54.800 --> 00:02:59.380
Now, the immediate question is, Will, how
how is the Trump electorate going to react?

00:02:59.380 --> 00:03:01.270
How are the Trump people going to react?

00:03:01.270 --> 00:03:03.280
Well, they're already doing it.

00:03:03.280 --> 00:03:06.040
They are saying the statistics are fake to
make them look bad.

00:03:06.040 --> 00:03:13.290
Now, that, of course, would require all sorts
of conspiracy involving a whole bunch of different

00:03:13.290 --> 00:03:17.940
agencies in multiple states, red and blue
states.

00:03:17.940 --> 00:03:24.330
The simpler explanation, a sort of casual
Occam's razor, is the data might just be real

00:03:24.330 --> 00:03:27.550
and it reflects what's happening within these
different places.

00:03:27.550 --> 00:03:28.550
That's the most intuitive.

00:03:28.550 --> 00:03:32.430
It requires the fewest assumptions and it's
the simplest explanation.

00:03:32.430 --> 00:03:36.380
So some people will claim the numbers are
just fake and they're made up.

00:03:36.380 --> 00:03:37.800
Others will just ignore the statistics.

00:03:37.800 --> 00:03:40.550
You know, it'll it'll and it could shift over
time.

00:03:40.550 --> 00:03:42.840
It might begin with denial.

00:03:42.840 --> 00:03:47.400
Then it will go to anger about the people
making up numbers to make red states look

00:03:47.400 --> 00:03:49.840
bad and then who knows?

00:03:49.840 --> 00:03:52.300
Or they might even invent something whole
cloth.

00:03:52.300 --> 00:03:56.930
You know, Biden is bringing infected immigrants
from other countries and releasing them into

00:03:56.930 --> 00:04:00.569
red states to drive up the numbers, something
like that.

00:04:00.569 --> 00:04:07.599
But the truth is, this is exactly what you
would expect based on the different behavior,

00:04:07.599 --> 00:04:11.420
the different attitudes and the different
vaccination rates.

00:04:11.420 --> 00:04:14.190
The other thing you might see, by the way,
the other thing you might see as a result

00:04:14.190 --> 00:04:19.780
of this is some of the red states just clamping
down on reporting this stuff.

00:04:19.780 --> 00:04:23.720
We're going to look at covid hell Florida
later.

00:04:23.720 --> 00:04:26.830
We still don't even know if we're getting
accurate numbers from Florida.

00:04:26.830 --> 00:04:31.630
The numbers we're getting are the worst in
the country and the worst that Florida has

00:04:31.630 --> 00:04:33.090
seen in the pandemic.

00:04:33.090 --> 00:04:36.389
Single day record, more than twenty four,
twenty one thousand cases in a single day

00:04:36.389 --> 00:04:38.200
over the weekend.

00:04:38.200 --> 00:04:42.490
We don't even know if these are truly the
numbers that are coming out of Florida.

00:04:42.490 --> 00:04:44.770
And given their track record, it's really
unclear.

00:04:44.770 --> 00:04:48.100
So it is wild what is going on right now.

00:04:48.100 --> 00:04:50.710
The world is looking on in horror.

00:04:50.710 --> 00:04:54.729
The vaccinated are looking at the unvaccinated
and saying, what are you doing?

00:04:54.729 --> 00:04:55.729
What are you doing?

00:04:55.729 --> 00:05:02.509
And I have actually a really sort of disturbing
voicemail today about how we've been talking.

